{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"laravel-config","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Laravel Config and Env","description":"Search and insert config('file.key') and env('KEY') from your real config files and .env, see what a key is set to, and find env() calls missing from .env.example.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Tools"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onCommand:laravelConfig.findConfig","onCommand:laravelConfig.findEnv","onCommand:laravelConfig.explain","onCommand:laravelConfig.openConfig","onCommand:laravelConfig.undefinedEnv"],"permissions":["workspace.read"],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"laravelConfig.findConfig","title":"Find Config Key...","category":"Laravel Config and Env"},{"command":"laravelConfig.findEnv","title":"Find Environment Variable...","category":"Laravel Config and Env"},{"command":"laravelConfig.explain","title":"What Is This Config Key Set To?","category":"Laravel Config and Env"},{"command":"laravelConfig.openConfig","title":"Open a Config File...","category":"Laravel Config and Env"},{"command":"laravelConfig.undefinedEnv","title":"Find env() Variables Missing from .env.example","category":"Laravel Config and Env"}]}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Laravel Config: find and insert config('file.key') and env('KEY') from your real config files and .env, see what a key is set to,\n// and catch env() calls whose variable is not in .env.example. Reads config/*.php and .env files as text.\n\n/** Flat dotted keys of a config file that `return [ ... ];` with their raw PHP values. */\nfunction parseConfig(text) {\n  const src = text.replace(/\\/\\*[\\s\\S]*?\\*\\//g, (m) => m.replace(/[^\\n]/g, ' ')).replace(/^\\s*(\\/\\/|#).*$/gm, '');\n  const out = {};\n  const ret = src.search(/return\\s*\\[/);\n  if (ret < 0) return out;\n  let i = src.indexOf('[', ret) + 1;\n  const stack = [''];\n  const skip = () => {\n    while (i < src.length && /[\\s,]/.test(src[i])) i++;\n  };\n  const readString = () => {\n    const q = src[i++];\n    let s = '';\n    while (i < src.length && src[i] !== q) {\n      if (src[i] === '\\\\') {\n        s += src[i] + src[i + 1];\n        i += 2;\n      } else s += src[i++];\n    }\n    i++;\n    return s;\n  };\n  const readValue = () => {\n    const start = i;\n    let depth = 0;\n    while (i < src.length) {\n      const c = src[i];\n      if (c === \"'\" || c === '\"') {\n        readString();\n        continue;\n      }\n      if (c === '(' || c === '[') depth++;\n      if (c === ')' || c === ']') {\n        if (depth === 0) break;\n        depth--;\n      }\n      if (c === ',' && depth === 0) break;\n      i++;\n    }\n    return src.slice(start, i).replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\n  };\n  while (i < src.length && stack.length) {\n    skip();\n    const c = src[i];\n    if (c === ']') {\n      stack.pop();\n      i++;\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (c === \"'\" || c === '\"') {\n      const key = readString();\n      skip();\n      if (src.startsWith('=>', i)) {\n        i += 2;\n        skip();\n        const path = stack[stack.length - 1] ? stack[stack.length - 1] + '.' + key : key;\n        if (src[i] === '[') {\n          i++;\n          stack.push(path);\n          out[path] = '[...]';\n        } else out[path] = readValue();\n      }\n      continue;\n    }\n    i++;\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\n/** KEY=value pairs of a .env text, with values hidden for names that look secret. */\nfunction parseEnv(text) {\n  const vars = {};\n  for (const line of text.replace(/\\r\\n/g, '\\n').split('\\n')) {\n    const m = /^\\s*(?:export\\s+)?([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_.]*)\\s*=\\s*(.*)$/.exec(line);\n    if (!m) continue;\n    let v = m[2];\n    const q = v[0];\n    if ((q === '\"' || q === \"'\") && v.lastIndexOf(q) > 0) v = v.slice(1, v.lastIndexOf(q));\n    else v = v.replace(/\\s+#.*$/, '').trim();\n    vars[m[1]] = v;\n  }\n  return vars;\n}\n\nconst SECRET = /(secret|token|password|passwd|key|credential|auth|signature|salt|dsn)/i;\nconst hide = (name, value) => (SECRET.test(name) && value ? '********' : value);\n\n/** env('KEY') and env('KEY', default) calls in PHP source. */\nfunction envCalls(source, file = '') {\n  const out = [];\n  const lines = source.split('\\n');\n  for (let i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {\n    for (const m of lines[i].matchAll(/\\benv\\(\\s*['\"]([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)['\"]\\s*(?:,\\s*([^)]*))?\\)/g)) out.push({ key: m[1], hasDefault: m[2] !== undefined, file, line: i + 1 });\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n\n/** The config('x.y') key the cursor is inside, on one line. */\nfunction configKeyAt(line, col) {\n  for (const m of line.matchAll(/\\bconfig\\(\\s*['\"]([\\w.\\-*]+)['\"]/g)) {\n    const start = m.index + m[0].indexOf(m[1]);\n    if (col >= start && col <= start + m[1].length) return m[1];\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\nexports._test = { parseConfig, parseEnv, envCalls, configKeyAt, hide };\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  const root = () => ferrum.workspace.root;\n  const sep = () => (root().includes('\\\\') ? '\\\\' : '/');\n  const full = (p) => (/^([a-zA-Z]:|[\\\\/])/.test(p) ? p : root() + sep() + p);\n  let configCache = null;\n\n  async function configKeys() {\n    if (configCache) return configCache;\n    const files = (await ferrum.workspace.listFiles('config/*.php')).filter((f) => /(^|[\\\\/])config[\\\\/][^\\\\/]+\\.php$/.test(f));\n    const all = [];\n    for (const f of files) {\n      const group = f.replace(/\\\\/g, '/').split('/').pop().replace(/\\.php$/, '');\n      let text;\n      try {\n        text = await ferrum.workspace.readFile(full(f));\n      } catch {\n        continue;\n      }\n      for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(parseConfig(text))) all.push({ key: group + '.' + k, value: v, file: f });\n    }\n    configCache = all;\n    return all;\n  }\n  async function readEnv(name) {\n    try {\n      return parseEnv(await ferrum.workspace.readFile(full(name)));\n    } catch {\n      return null;\n    }\n  }\n\n  context.subscriptions.push(\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelConfig.findConfig', async () => {\n      if (!root()) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open the Laravel project folder first.', 'warn');\n      const keys = (await configKeys()).filter((k) => k.value !== '[...]');\n      if (!keys.length) return ferrum.window.showMessage('No config files found in config/.', 'warn');\n      const p = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(keys.map((k, i) => ({ label: k.key, detail: k.value, i })), { placeholder: 'Search config keys' });\n      if (p) await ferrum.editor.insert(\"config('\" + keys[p.i].key + \"')\");\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelConfig.findEnv', async () => {\n      if (!root()) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open the Laravel project folder first.', 'warn');\n      const a = (await readEnv('.env.example')) || {};\n      const b = (await readEnv('.env')) || {};\n      const names = [...new Set([...Object.keys(a), ...Object.keys(b)])].sort();\n      if (!names.length) return ferrum.window.showMessage('No .env or .env.example found.', 'warn');\n      const p = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(names.map((n) => ({ label: n, detail: hide(n, n in b ? b[n] : a[n]) + (n in b ? '' : '   (only in .env.example)') })), { placeholder: 'Search environment variables' });\n      if (!p) return;\n      await ferrum.editor.insert(\"env('\" + p.label + \"')\");\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelConfig.explain', async () => {\n      const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n      if (!doc) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a PHP or Blade file first.', 'warn');\n      const line = await ferrum.editor.getLine(doc.selection.start.line);\n      const key = doc.selectedText && /^[\\w.\\-]+$/.test(doc.selectedText.trim()) ? doc.selectedText.trim() : configKeyAt(line, doc.selection.start.col);\n      if (!key) return ferrum.window.showMessage(\"Put the cursor inside config('...') or select a key like app.name.\", 'warn');\n      const hit = (await configKeys()).find((k) => k.key === key);\n      if (!hit) return ferrum.window.showMessage(key + ' is not defined in config/*.php.', 'warn');\n      ferrum.window.showMessage(key + ' = ' + hit.value + '   (' + hit.file + ')');\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelConfig.openConfig', async () => {\n      const keys = await configKeys();\n      const groups = [...new Set(keys.map((k) => k.file))].sort();\n      if (!groups.length) return ferrum.window.showMessage('No config files found.', 'warn');\n      const p = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(groups.map((f) => ({ label: f.replace(/\\\\/g, '/').split('/').pop(), detail: f, f })), { placeholder: 'Open a config file' });\n      if (p) await ferrum.editor.openFile(full(p.f));\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelConfig.undefinedEnv', async () => {\n      if (!root()) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open the Laravel project folder first.', 'warn');\n      const example = await readEnv('.env.example');\n      if (!example) return ferrum.window.showMessage('There is no .env.example to compare with.', 'warn');\n      const files = (await ferrum.workspace.listFiles()).filter((f) => /^(app|config|routes|database)[\\\\/].*\\.php$/.test(f.replace(/\\\\/g, '/')) || /^(app|config|routes|database)\\/.*\\.php$/.test(f.replace(/\\\\/g, '/')));\n      const calls = [];\n      for (const f of files) {\n        try {\n          calls.push(...envCalls(await ferrum.workspace.readFile(full(f)), f));\n        } catch {\n          /* skip */\n        }\n      }\n      const missing = new Map();\n      for (const c of calls) if (!(c.key in example) && !missing.has(c.key)) missing.set(c.key, c);\n      if (!missing.size) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Every env() variable used in the code is listed in .env.example.');\n      const p = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick([...missing.values()].map((c) => ({ label: c.key, detail: c.file + ':' + c.line + (c.hasDefault ? '   (has a default)' : '   (no default)'), c })), { placeholder: missing.size + ' env() variables are not in .env.example. Pick one to open.' });\n      if (p) await ferrum.editor.openFile(full(p.c.file), { line: p.c.line - 1, col: 0 });\n    }),\n    ferrum.events.on('save', (d) => {\n      if (d && /config[\\\\/][^\\\\/]+\\.php$/.test(d.path || '')) configCache = null;\n    }),\n  );\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Laravel Config and Env\n\n- **Find Config Key...** lists every key of `config/*.php` with its value as written (`env('APP_NAME', 'Laravel')`), and inserts `config('app.name')`.\n- **Find Environment Variable...** lists the names in `.env` and `.env.example`. Values of names that look secret (password, token, key...) are hidden. Inserts `env('NAME')`.\n- **What Is This Config Key Set To?** put the cursor inside `config('services.stripe.key')` and run it: it shows the definition line in the config file.\n- **Open a Config File...** jumps to one of the files in `config/`.\n- **Find env() Variables Missing from .env.example** scans `app/`, `config/`, `routes/` and `database/` for `env('X')` and lists the ones .env.example does not have, so a new developer is not surprised. Pick one to open it.\n\nPermission: workspace.read. Nothing is sent anywhere.\n"}}}